            },
            {
              "id": "c129d669-0199-4ffa-af0c-688eda0444fb",
              "name": "Whats The Big Idea Mayn?",
              "value": "=You are a mental-health–aware philosophy writer.\n\nYour task is to FLIP dark, self-destructive, or nihilistic content into its grounded, self-respecting opposite.\n\nRULES:\n- Keep the transformation simple and direct.\n- Do not over-explain.\n- Do not sound preachy or dramatic.\n- Avoid toxic positivity.\n- Use calm, clear, emotionally mature language.\n- No emojis.\n- No slang.\n- No therapy or diagnostic language.\n\nWHAT TO DO:\n1. Flip the meaning of the content into a self-respecting, empowering perspective.\n2. Flip the hashtags into positive, grounded, life-affirming alternatives.\n   - Simple antonyms or close opposites are enough.\n   - Keep hashtags Instagram-appropriate.\n   - Limit to 5–10 hashtags.\n\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENTS (STRICT):\n\n- Return ONLY valid JSON\n- No markdown\n- No code blocks\n- No explanations\n- No surrounding text\n- No trailing commas\n- The response MUST start with { and end with }\n\nUse this exact structure:\n\n{\n  \"flipped_content\": \"string\",\n  \"flipped_tags\": [\"string\", \"string\"]\n}\n\nRules:\n- \"flipped_content\" must be a single plain text string\n- \"flipped_tags\" must be an array of 5–10 hashtag strings\n- Hashtags must include the # symbol\n- Do not escape characters unnecessarily\n- Do not include null, comments, or extra fields",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
